/**
 * @file feature_analysis.hpp
 * @brief Defines classes and functions for feature analysis across systems.
 *
 * @page feature_analysis Feature Analysis System
 *
 * @tableofcontents
 *
 * @section introduction Introduction
 *
 * This library provides tools for analyzing features across different systems.
 * It allows for the generation, categorization, and analysis of all possible combinations
 * of features, including fundamental features and derived features created through logical
 * operations (AND, OR) and negations.
 *
 * @section components Key Components
 *
 * - **Namespace `feature_isolation`:** Contains all classes and functions related to feature analysis.
 * - **Class `feature_isolation::feature_analysis_t`:** Main class that performs feature generation and analysis.
 * - **Class `feature_isolation::system_t`:** Represents a single system with associated features.
 * - **Feature Categories:** Constants and utilities for handling different types of features.
 * - **Helper Functions:**
 *   - `feature_isolation::to_string(const feature_t&)`: Converts a feature to its string representation.
 *   - `feature_isolation::separator(const char s = 0)`: Provides a customizable separator character for output formatting.
 *
 * @section usage Usage
 *
 * 1. Include the header:
 *    ```cpp
 *    #include "feature_analysis.hpp"
 *    ```
 * 2. Create an instance of `feature_analysis_t`:
 *    ```cpp
 *    feature_isolation::feature_analysis_t analysis(F, R, feature_categories);
 *    ```
 *    - `F`: Number of fundamental features.
 *    - `R`: Maximum rank for feature combinations.
 *    - `feature_categories`: Bitmask of feature categories to include (e.g., `feature_isolation::ALL`).
 * 3. Perform analysis and output results:
 *    ```cpp
 *    analysis.print(std::cout);
 *    ```
 *
 * @section example Example
 *
 * ```cpp
 * #include <iostream>
 * #include "feature_analysis.hpp"
 *
 * int main() {
 *   using namespace feature_isolation;
 *
 *   unsigned_integer F = 3; // Number of fundamental features
 *   unsigned_integer R = 2; // Maximum rank for combinations
 *
 *   feature_analysis_t analysis(F, R);
 *   analysis.print(std::cout);
 *
 *   return 0;
 * }
 * ```
 *
 * The following is a sample output for the example code provided above:
 * ```
 * 	F	N	A	O	AN	ON	ANF	ONF	DF	T	S	R	C
 * IN PRINCIPLE	3	3	4	4	4	4	6	6	31	34	8	3	F|N|A|O|AN|ON|ANF|ONF
 * ACTUALLY	3	3	3	3	3	3	6	6	27	30	8	2	F|N|A|O|AN|ON|ANF|ONF
 * 
 * SYSTEM ID	F	N	A	O	AN	ON	ANF	ONF
 * 1		4 5 6 			13 14 15 	16 17 18 		25 26 27 28 29 30
 * 2	1 	5 6 		10 11 	15 	16 17 18 	19 	25 26 27 28 29
 * 3	2 	4 6 		10 12 	14 	16 17 18 	20 	25 26 27 28 30
 * 4	1 2 	6 	7 	10 11 12 		17 18 	22 	25 26 28 29 30
 * 5	3 	4 5 		11 12 	13 	16 17 18 	21 	25 26 27 29 30
 * 6	1 3 	5 	8 	10 11 12 		16 18 	23 	25 27 28 29 30
 * 7	2 3 	4 	9 	10 11 12 		16 17 	24 	26 27 28 29 30
 * 8	1 2 3 		7 8 9 	10 11 12 				25 26 27 28 29 30
 * ``` 
 *
 * **Customization:**
 * - Control the categories of features included by adjusting the `feature_categories` parameter.
 * - Customize the output separator using the `separator` function.
 */

/**
 * @file feature_analysis.hpp
 * @brief Provides classes and functions for feature analysis across systems.
 *
 * @details
 * This header defines classes and functions that allow for the creation and analysis
 * of features over a set of systems. It includes the generation of fundamental and
 * derived features, categorization, and statistical analysis of feature distribution
 * across systems.
 *
 * **Key Components:**
 * - **Namespace `feature_isolation`:** Encapsulates all functionality related to feature analysis.
 * - **Class `feature_analysis_t`:** Main class that performs feature generation and analysis.
 * - **Class `system_t`:** Represents a single system with associated features.
 * - **Feature Categories:** Constants and utilities for handling different types of features.
 */

/**
 * @class feature_isolation::system_t
 * @brief Represents a system with associated features in various categories.
 *
 * @details
 * Stores feature IDs for each category present in the system and provides methods
 * to calculate derived statistics.
 *
 * **Member Variables:**
 * - `F_feature_ids`: Fundamental feature IDs.
 * - `N_feature_ids`: Negated fundamental feature IDs.
 * - `A_feature_ids`: AND combination feature IDs.
 * - `O_feature_ids`: OR combination feature IDs.
 * - `AN_feature_ids`: AND of negated features IDs.
 * - `ON_feature_ids`: OR of negated features IDs.
 * - `ANF_feature_ids`: AND combinations of fundamental and negated features IDs.
 * - `ONF_feature_ids`: OR combinations of fundamental and negated features IDs.
 *
 * **Member Functions:**
 * - `unsigned_integer T() const`: Calculates the total number of features in the system.
 * - `unsigned_integer DF() const`: Calculates the total number of derived features.
 * - `feature_ids_t all_features() const`: Aggregates all feature IDs from all categories.
 */

/**
 * @var feature_isolation::system_t::F_feature_ids
 * @brief Set of fundamental feature IDs present in the system.
 *
 * @details
 * Contains the IDs of fundamental features that are active in this system.
 */

/**
 * @var feature_isolation::system_t::N_feature_ids
 * @brief Set of negated fundamental feature IDs present in the system.
 *
 * @details
 * Contains the IDs of negated fundamental features that are active in this system.
 */

/**
 * @var feature_isolation::system_t::A_feature_ids
 * @brief Set of AND combination feature IDs present in the system.
 *
 * @details
 * Contains the IDs of features formed by logical AND of fundamental features.
 */

/**
 * @var feature_isolation::system_t::O_feature_ids
 * @brief Set of OR combination feature IDs present in the system.
 *
 * @details
 * Contains the IDs of features formed by logical OR of fundamental features.
 */

/**
 * @var feature_isolation::system_t::AN_feature_ids
 * @brief Set of AND of negated features IDs present in the system.
 *
 * @details
 * Contains the IDs of features formed by logical AND of negated fundamental features.
 */

/**
 * @var feature_isolation::system_t::ON_feature_ids
 * @brief Set of OR of negated features IDs present in the system.
 *
 * @details
 * Contains the IDs of features formed by logical OR of negated fundamental features.
 */

/**
 * @var feature_isolation::system_t::ANF_feature_ids
 * @brief Set of AND combinations of fundamental and negated features IDs present in the system.
 *
 * @details
 * Contains the IDs of features formed by logical AND of a mix of fundamental and negated features.
 */

/**
 * @var feature_isolation::system_t::ONF_feature_ids
 * @brief Set of OR combinations of fundamental and negated features IDs present in the system.
 *
 * @details
 * Contains the IDs of features formed by logical OR of a mix of fundamental and negated features.
 */

/**
 * @fn [[nodiscard]] unsigned_integer feature_isolation::system_t::T() const
 * @brief Calculates the total number of features (fundamental + derived) in the system.
 *
 * @return The total number of features present in the system.
 *
 * @details
 * Computes the sum of fundamental features and derived features (`F_feature_ids.size() + DF()`).
 */

/**
 * @fn [[nodiscard]] unsigned_integer feature_isolation::system_t::DF() const
 * @brief Calculates the total number of derived features in the system.
 *
 * @return The number of derived features.
 *
 * @details
 * Adds up the sizes of all derived feature ID sets (`N_feature_ids`, `A_feature_ids`, etc.).
 */

/**
 * @fn [[nodiscard]] feature_ids_t feature_isolation::system_t::all_features() const
 * @brief Aggregates all feature IDs from all categories into a single set.
 *
 * @return A set of all feature IDs present in the system.
 *
 * @details
 * Merges all feature ID sets into one `feature_ids_t` set.
 */

//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////

/**
 * @class feature_isolation::feature_analysis_t
 * @brief Main class for performing feature analysis across systems.
 *
 * @details
 * Generates fundamental and derived features, categorizes them, and assigns them
 * to systems based on their presence. Provides methods to output detailed analysis
 * and statistics.
 *
 * **Constructor:**
 * ```cpp
 * feature_analysis_t(unsigned_integer f, unsigned_integer max_rank, unsigned_integer feature_categories_ = ::feature_isolation::ALL);
 * ```
 * - `f`: Number of fundamental features.
 * - `max_rank`: Maximum rank for feature combinations.
 * - `feature_categories_`: Bitmask indicating which feature categories to include.
 *
 * **Member Functions:**
 * - `feature_t at(unsigned_integer feature_id) const`: Retrieves the feature corresponding to a given feature ID.
 * - `unsigned_integer category(unsigned_integer feature_id) const`: Determines the category index for a given feature ID.
 * - `std::string category_name(unsigned_integer feature_id) const`: Retrieves the name of the feature category based on the feature ID.
 * - `void print_feature(std::ostream& os, const feature_t& feature) const`: Outputs a single feature's representation to a stream.
 * - `void print_features(std::ostream& os) const`: Outputs all features, their IDs, categories, and descriptions.
 * - `void print_categories(std::ostream& os) const`: Outputs the active feature categories based on the category bitmask.
 * - `void print_system_statistics(std::ostream& os, const system_t& system, unsigned_integer id) const`: Outputs statistics for a single system.
 * - `void print_systems_statistics(std::ostream& os) const`: Outputs statistics for all systems.
 * - `void print_system_features(std::ostream& os, const system_t& system, unsigned_integer system_id) const`: Outputs feature IDs present in each category for a single system.
 * - `void print_systems_features(std::ostream& os) const`: Outputs feature IDs for all systems.
 * - `void print(std::ostream& os) const`: Outputs a comprehensive summary of the feature analysis.
 *
 * **Member Variables:**
 * - `unsigned_integer F`: Number of fundamental features.
 * - `unsigned_integer N`: Number of negated fundamental features.
 * - `unsigned_integer A`: Number of AND combinations.
 * - `unsigned_integer O`: Number of OR combinations.
 * - `unsigned_integer AN`: Number of AND of negated features.
 * - `unsigned_integer ON`: Number of OR of negated features.
 * - `unsigned_integer ANF`: Number of AND combinations of fundamental and negated features.
 * - `unsigned_integer ONF`: Number of OR combinations of fundamental and negated features.
 * - `unsigned_integer DF`: Total number of derived features.
 * - `unsigned_integer T`: Total number of features.
 * - `unsigned_integer R`: Maximum rank for combinations.
 * - `unsigned_integer C`: Feature categories bitmask.
 * - `unsigned_integer S`: Total number of systems (`2^F`).
 * - Feature vectors: `F_features`, `N_features`, `A_features`, `O_features`, `AN_features`, `ON_features`, `ANF_features`, `ONF_features`.
 * - Feature ID offsets: `F_offset`, `N_offset`, `A_offset`, `O_offset`, `AN_offset`, `ON_offset`, `ANF_offset`, `ONF_offset`.
 * - `std::vector<unsigned_integer> m_feature_offsets`: Offsets for feature IDs in categories.
 * - `std::vector<features_t*> m_all_features`: Pointers to all feature vectors.
 * - `systems_t m_systems`: Vector of systems with assigned features.
 */

//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////

/**
 * @fn feature_isolation::feature_analysis_t::feature_analysis_t(unsigned_integer f, unsigned_integer max_rank, unsigned_integer feature_categories_)
 * @brief Constructs a new `feature_analysis_t` object with the specified parameters.
 *
 * @param f The number of fundamental features.
 * @param max_rank The maximum rank for feature combinations.
 * @param feature_categories_ Bitmask indicating which feature categories to include. Default is `::feature_isolation::ALL`.
 *
 * @details
 * Initializes the feature analysis by generating fundamental features and derived features based on the specified parameters.
 * Sets up internal data structures for feature offsets and system representations.
 *
 * **Member Variable Initialization:**
 * - Calculates counts for each feature category (`F`, `N`, `A`, `O`, `AN`, `ON`, `ANF`, `ONF`).
 * - Calculates total derived features (`DF`) and total features (`T`).
 * - Initializes feature vectors by calling initialization functions.
 * - Sets up feature ID offsets for quick access.
 * - Initializes systems with assigned features.
 *
 * @throws std::invalid_argument if `max_rank` exceeds the number of fundamental features.
 */

//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////

/**
 * @fn [[nodiscard]] feature_t feature_isolation::feature_analysis_t::at(unsigned_integer feature_id) const
 * @brief Retrieves the feature corresponding to a given feature ID.
 *
 * @param feature_id The global feature ID.
 * @return The feature associated with the given ID.
 *
 * @details
 * Determines the category of the feature based on `feature_id`, then accesses the corresponding feature vector to retrieve the feature.
 */

/**
 * @fn [[nodiscard]] unsigned_integer feature_isolation::feature_analysis_t::category(unsigned_integer feature_id) const
 * @brief Determines the category index for a given feature ID.
 *
 * @param feature_id The global feature ID.
 * @return The category index (0 to 7).
 *
 * @details
 * Uses the feature ID offsets to find out which category the feature belongs to.
 */

/**
 * @fn [[nodiscard]] std::string feature_isolation::feature_analysis_t::category_name(unsigned_integer feature_id) const
 * @brief Retrieves the name of the feature category based on the feature ID.
 *
 * @param feature_id The global feature ID.
 * @return The name of the feature category.
 *
 * @details
 * Calls `category(feature_id)` to get the category index, then returns the corresponding category name from `feature_categories`.
 */

/**
 * @fn void feature_isolation::feature_analysis_t::print_feature(std::ostream& os, const feature_t& feature) const
 * @brief Outputs a single feature's representation to a stream.
 *
 * @param os The output stream.
 * @param feature The feature to print.
 *
 * @details
 * Uses `to_string(const feature_t&)` to convert the feature to a string and writes it to the output stream.
 */

/**
 * @fn void feature_isolation::feature_analysis_t::print_features(std::ostream& os) const
 * @brief Outputs all features, their IDs, categories, and descriptions.
 *
 * @param os The output stream.
 *
 * @details
 * Iterates over all active feature categories and prints each feature's ID, category, and description.
 */

/**
 * @fn void feature_isolation::feature_analysis_t::print_categories(std::ostream& os) const
 * @brief Outputs the active feature categories based on the category bitmask.
 *
 * @param os The output stream.
 *
 * @details
 * Prints a string representation of the active feature categories, using '|' as a separator.
 * Active categories are shown by their abbreviations; inactive ones are replaced with '-'.
 */

/**
 * @fn void feature_isolation::feature_analysis_t::print_system_statistics(std::ostream& os, const system_t& system, unsigned_integer id) const
 * @brief Outputs statistics for a single system.
 *
 * @param os The output stream.
 * @param system The system to analyze.
 * @param id The system ID.
 *
 * @details
 * Prints the counts of features in each category for the given system, along with total derived features and total features.
 */

/**
 * @fn void feature_isolation::feature_analysis_t::print_systems_statistics(std::ostream& os) const
 * @brief Outputs statistics for all systems.
 *
 * @param os The output stream.
 *
 * @details
 * Iterates over all systems and calls `print_system_statistics` for each one.
 */

/**
 * @fn void feature_isolation::feature_analysis_t::print_system_features(std::ostream& os, const system_t& system, unsigned_integer system_id) const
 * @brief Outputs feature IDs present in each category for a single system.
 *
 * @param os The output stream.
 * @param system The system to analyze.
 * @param system_id The system ID.
 *
 * @details
 * For each feature category, prints the feature IDs that are active in the given system.
 */

/**
 * @fn void feature_isolation::feature_analysis_t::print_systems_features(std::ostream& os) const
 * @brief Outputs feature IDs for all systems.
 *
 * @param os The output stream.
 *
 * @details
 * Iterates over all systems and calls `print_system_features` for each one.
 */

/**
 * @fn void feature_isolation::feature_analysis_t::print(std::ostream& os) const
 * @brief Outputs a comprehensive summary of the feature analysis.
 *
 * @param os The output stream.
 *
 * @details
 * Prints overall statistics, including counts of features in principle and actually generated.
 * Outputs system features and additional analysis results.
 */

//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////

/**
 * @fn [[nodiscard]] features_t feature_isolation::feature_analysis_t::initialize_F_features() const
 * @brief Initializes the fundamental features.
 *
 * @return A vector of fundamental features (`features_t`).
 *
 * @details
 * Generates all fundamental features by setting each feature to alternate between `true` and `false` over the systems.
 * Each fundamental feature corresponds to a single fundamental property.
 */

/**
 * @fn [[nodiscard]] features_t feature_isolation::feature_analysis_t::initialize_N_features() const
 * @brief Initializes the negations of fundamental features.
 *
 * @return A vector of negated fundamental features (`features_t`).
 *
 * @details
 * Generates negated fundamental features by flipping the values of each fundamental feature.
 */

/**
 * @fn void feature_isolation::feature_analysis_t::and_combine(feature_t& f1, const feature_t& f2) const
 * @brief Performs logical AND between two features and stores the result in the first feature.
 *
 * @param f1 The first feature (will be modified).
 * @param f2 The second feature.
 *
 * @details
 * Iterates over both features and applies logical AND to each corresponding element.
 */

/**
 * @fn [[nodiscard]] features_t feature_isolation::feature_analysis_t::initialize_A_features() const
 * @brief Initializes the AND combinations of fundamental features.
 *
 * @return A vector of AND combination features (`features_t`).
 *
 * @throws std::invalid_argument if `R` exceeds the number of fundamental features.
 *
 * @details
 * Generates all possible logical AND combinations of fundamental features up to rank `R`.
 * Uses combinations of feature indices to create higher-order features.
 */

/**
 * @fn void feature_isolation::feature_analysis_t::or_combine(feature_t& f1, const feature_t& f2) const
 * @brief Performs logical OR between two features and stores the result in the first feature.
 *
 * @param f1 The first feature (will be modified).
 * @param f2 The second feature.
 *
 * @details
 * Iterates over both features and applies logical OR to each corresponding element.
 */

/**
 * @fn [[nodiscard]] features_t feature_isolation::feature_analysis_t::initialize_O_features() const
 * @brief Initializes the OR combinations of fundamental features.
 *
 * @return A vector of OR combination features (`features_t`).
 *
 * @throws std::invalid_argument if `R` exceeds the number of fundamental features.
 *
 * @details
 * Generates all possible logical OR combinations of fundamental features up to rank `R`.
 */

/**
 * @fn [[nodiscard]] features_t feature_isolation::feature_analysis_t::initialize_AN_features() const
 * @brief Initializes the AND combinations of negated fundamental features.
 *
 * @return A vector of AND of negated features (`features_t`).
 *
 * @throws std::invalid_argument if `R` exceeds the number of fundamental features.
 *
 * @details
 * Generates all possible logical AND combinations of negated fundamental features up to rank `R`.
 */

/**
 * @fn [[nodiscard]] features_t feature_isolation::feature_analysis_t::initialize_ON_features() const
 * @brief Initializes the OR combinations of negated fundamental features.
 *
 * @return A vector of OR of negated features (`features_t`).
 *
 * @throws std::invalid_argument if `R` exceeds the number of fundamental features.
 *
 * @details
 * Generates all possible logical OR combinations of negated fundamental features up to rank `R`.
 */

/**
 * @fn [[nodiscard]] features_t feature_isolation::feature_analysis_t::initialize_ANF_features() const
 * @brief Initializes the AND combinations of fundamental and negated features.
 *
 * @return A vector of AND combinations mixing fundamental and negated features (`features_t`).
 *
 * @details
 * Generates all possible logical AND combinations that mix fundamental features and their negations, excluding the combination where all features are negated.
 */

/**
 * @fn [[nodiscard]] features_t feature_isolation::feature_analysis_t::initialize_ONF_features() const
 * @brief Initializes the OR combinations of fundamental and negated features.
 *
 * @return A vector of OR combinations mixing fundamental and negated features (`features_t`).
 *
 * @details
 * Generates all possible logical OR combinations that mix fundamental features and their negations, excluding the combination where all features are negated.
 */

/**
 * @fn void feature_isolation::feature_analysis_t::insert_id(systems_t& systems, const feature_t& feature, unsigned_integer feature_id, unsigned_integer category) const
 * @brief Inserts a feature ID into the appropriate category set for systems where the feature is present.
 *
 * @param systems The vector of systems to update.
 * @param feature The feature indicating presence (`true`) in systems.
 * @param feature_id The ID of the feature to insert.
 * @param category The category of the feature.
 *
 * @details
 * Iterates over the feature's values and, for each system where the feature is `true`, adds the feature ID to the corresponding category set in the system.
 */

/**
 * @fn systems_t feature_isolation::feature_analysis_t::initialize_systems() const
 * @brief Initializes the systems with assigned features based on the analysis.
 *
 * @return A vector of systems with features assigned.
 *
 * @details
 * For each feature in all active categories, determines in which systems the feature is present and updates the systems accordingly.
 * Reverses the system IDs to match the desired ordering.
 */

//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////

